<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!-- The Debug half of a two-file split. The shipping set lives in
     GetHogMac-Distribution.entitlements, which adds the App Group and the
     shared keychain group; project.yml selects it for Release. Read that file
     first — it carries the memberships, this one carries the subtraction.

     Why Debug is short: either group entitlement, alone, makes a macOS target
     refuse to build without a development certificate ("GetHogMac has
     entitlements that require signing with a development certificate" —
     measured by adding each separately and building), and `DEVELOPMENT_TEAM`
     is empty here because a team id is an account detail, not a project fact
     (DEVELOPMENT.md, "App Store archive and signing"). A fresh clone builds
     Debug, so Debug is the configuration that has to survive having no
     certificate. iOS never met this: a Simulator build is not signed against a
     profile.

     Nothing in a Debug run needs the groups. `KeychainTokenStore` takes its
     access group as an argument and defaults to none, and `SharedSnapshotStore`
     resolves the App Group container and falls back to the app's own when there
     is not one — so a debug Mac app reads and writes its own credential and its
     own snapshot. What makes a *shared* group mean anything is a second
     process, and there is no macOS widget extension yet. -->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>com.apple.security.app-sandbox</key>
	<true/>
	<key>com.apple.security.network.client</key>
	<true/>
</dict>
</plist>
